invariant: INV-17
file: src/gcm_vaes.c
catches: ghash_equiv_test
reason: gcm_seal_passes_vaes returns without the wipe below its body, so the hash
  subkey's powers, the last pass's sums and its keystream stay in the
  stack. bin/ghash_equiv_test looks for each below the call on an x86-64
  CPU with the instructions (docs/decisions.md 182).

--- old
    seal_steps(round_keys, rounds, counter, acc, subkey, in, passes, out);
    gcm_hw_wipe_below();
--- new
    seal_steps(round_keys, rounds, counter, acc, subkey, in, passes, out);
